{"step_index":5764,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T20:29:06Z","thinking":"Normalization of Arabic/Persian/Urdu characters is required within a preprocessing stage. This involves specific character mappings to standardize these scripts. These mappings are: `گ`, `ک` to `ك`; `پ` to `ب`; `چ` to `ج`; `ژ` to `ز`; `ڤ` to `ف`; and handling the letter `ی`.\n\n\nA preprocessing stage is implemented to standardize Arabic text. Character mappings include: `ى` to `ي`, `ة` to `ه`, `أ`, `إ`, `آ`, `ٱ` to `ا`, correction of common spelling errors, and conversion of Persian/Hindi numerals to Western digits. This stage ensures consistent input for the entire pipeline.\n\n\nThe system must check if the LLM's matched classifications involve incompatible forms like injectables vs. tablets, sprays vs. gels, drops vs. tablets, or syrup vs. tablets. If so, a 'Review' status must be forced. A strict concentration check must also be implemented to reject any concentration discrepancies, overriding LLM's acceptance. User feedback suggests storing submitted messages to facilitate evaluation of prior LLM responses during future interactions, enabling filtering after the evaluation process.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"D:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\src\\match\\text_match.py","EndLine":100,"StartLine":1,"toolAction":"Viewing text_match.py","toolSummary":"View text_match.py"}}]}
