{"step_index":5794,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T20:30:51Z","thinking":"Considering vowel variations in Arabic prefixes like `جن` vs `جي`, the key is identifying the *first consonant*. Removing potential vowel letters like `ا`, `و`, `ي` reveals the underlying consonant. This approach applies similarly to `بروتولوك` whose first consonant is `ب`. Thus, the first consonant of `كونترولوك` is deduced as `ك`.\n\n\nA similarity threshold is established using the fuzz ratio, aiming for a minimum of 75% to identify likely matches, while considering that genuine OCR errors typically exceed 80%. When discrepancies are identified, a check for \"neo\" in the name or item is implemented to address variations of \"new\". A \"no_match\" status is set if the first consonants don't match, while excluding the letters that are vowels.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"& \"D:\\miniconda3\\envs\\venv\\python.exe\" -c \"\nconfusables = {'ب', 'ت', 'ث', 'ن', 'ي'}\ndef is_valid_brand_match(r, w):\n    r_c = r[2:] if r.startswith('ال') else r\n    w_c = w[2:] if w.startswith('ال') else w\n    if r_c and w_c and r_c[0] != w_c[0]:\n        if not (r_c[0] in confusables and w_c[0] in confusables):\n            return False\n    return True\n\ntests = [\n    ('بروتولوك', 'كونترولوك'),\n    ('نيوكاربون', 'اوكاربون'),\n    ('زنكترون', 'زنكتون'),\n    ('كارنيفيتا', 'كارنتينا'),\n    ('جنتازون', 'جينتازون'),\n    ('بروفين', 'برونفين'),\n    ('زيثروماكس', 'زيثرون')\n]\nfor r, w in tests:\n    print(f'{r} vs {w}: {is_valid_brand_match(r, w)}')\n\"","Cwd":"D:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy","IsDaemon":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Testing brand first letter rule","toolSummary":"Test brand first letter rule"}}]}
